IMPORT prelude

-- Bretton Woods Agreements Act 1966 (Singapore) -- who pays for Singapore's membership of the International Monetary Fund and the
-- International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (ss 4 to 10), when the Monetary Authority of Singapore may lend or give
-- grants in support of a Fund arrangement or program and what such an agreement must contain (s 6A), the US$40 million ceiling on
-- the Bank subscription (s 7(3)), orders giving the Fund and Bank Agreements the force of law (s 11), the Companies Act exemption
-- for the Bank's securities (s 12), and the terms of admission in the First and Second Schedules (quota, subscription, the par
-- value deadline, exchange transactions, and the steps to membership).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BWAA1966.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; its page footer reads "Informal
-- Consolidation - version in force from 11/12/2023", and the latest amending Act in its Legislative History is Act 20 of 2023
-- (Bretton Woods Agreements (Amendment) Act 2023, commenced 11 December 2023), annotated against ss 5(2), 6A(3A) and 6A(5). The SSO
-- metadata beside it reads "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026". Section numbers follow the BODY: the arrangement at the top of the
-- deposit is out of step (it lists "1." with no heading and puts every heading against the next number).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0160 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. Honest answer: almost nothing directly. The Act is about the State's membership of two international
-- bodies; a person meets it only through s 12 (the Bank's bonds are outside the Companies Act) and through any order under s 11.
-- The Act is short, so most of it is encoded. Not encoded: the short title, the s 2 authority to sign, the definitions (used, not
-- modelled), the MAS's SDR and General Resources Account powers in ss 5 and 6 beyond who pays, the Fund and Bank Articles of
-- Agreement themselves (not deposited), any order made under s 11 (none retrieved), and the acceptance windows in First Schedule
-- para 9 and Second Schedule para 7 (spent in 1966).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Bretton Woods Agreements Act 1966 -- membership`

§§ `4 to 10 -- who pays, and who must concur`

-- s 4(1): "It shall be the function of the Monetary Authority of Singapore to pay to the Fund the subscription"; (2) MAS may, "with
-- the approval of the Minister for Finance", accept an increase in the Fund subscription; (3) MAS "is hereby authorised to create and
-- issue to the Fund" non-interest bearing, non-negotiable notes in place of Singapore currency.
-- ss 5, 6: MAS pays SDR charges and General Resources Account charges and receives interest and remuneration. s 6A: MAS lends or
-- gives grants "on behalf of the Government".
-- s 7(1), (2): "There shall be charged on the Consolidated Fund" the Bank subscription and any increase payable in gold, US dollars
-- or Singapore currency; s 7(4): the Minister for Finance "with the President's concurrence under Article 144(1)(b) of the
-- Constitution" may issue notes to the Bank. s 8: charged on the Consolidated Fund -- (a) sums payable under Article II s 9 of the
-- Bank Agreement (changes in par value) and (b) redemption of notes issued to the Bank. s 9: the Minister, with the President's
-- concurrence, may raise loans for any payment under either Agreement; principal, interest and charges "charged on and paid out of
-- the Consolidated Fund". s 10: moneys received from the Bank are paid into the Consolidated Fund.
--
-- The Bank side is a charge on the Consolidated Fund; the Fund side is a function of the MAS.
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `the IMF subscription`
    `an increase in the IMF subscription`
    `charges on special drawing rights`
    `charges on the General Resources Account`
    `a loan or grant supporting a Fund arrangement`
    `the World Bank subscription`
    `an increase in the World Bank subscription`
    `a World Bank par value adjustment`
    `redemption of notes issued to the World Bank`
    `interest on a loan raised under section 9`

DECLARE Payer IS ONE OF
    `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    `the Consolidated Fund`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A Payer
`who bears the payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `the IMF subscription` THEN `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    WHEN `an increase in the IMF subscription` THEN `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    WHEN `charges on special drawing rights` THEN `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    WHEN `charges on the General Resources Account` THEN `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    WHEN `a loan or grant supporting a Fund arrangement` THEN `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    OTHERWISE `the Consolidated Fund`

DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `notes issued to the IMF`
    `notes issued to the World Bank`
    `a loan raised to pay either body`
    `an increase in the IMF quota`

-- Who must act or approve: s 4(3) authorises the MAS itself; s 4(2) needs the Minister for Finance's approval; under ss 7(4) and 9 the
-- Minister acts himself and needs the President's concurrence under Article 144(1)(b) of the Constitution.
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President must concur` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `notes issued to the World Bank` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a loan raised to pay either body` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister for Finance must act or approve` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `an increase in the IMF quota` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `notes issued to the World Bank` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a loan raised to pay either body` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6A -- assistance in support of a Fund arrangement or Fund program`

-- s 6A(1): MAS may, on behalf of the Government, "enter into an agreement (whether multilateral or bilateral) to lend, or give grants
-- or other financial assistance". (2) Only if -- (a) "the Fund requests Singapore to provide assistance"; (b) MAS "is satisfied that
-- at least one other government has provided, or intends to provide, financial assistance in response to a similar request"; (c)
-- "the Minister has published in the Gazette a statement" of the nature of the agreement and the maximum amount; and (d) "in the case
-- of grants, Parliament has, by a resolution, fixed the maximum amount of grants". (3A) [Act 20 of 2023]: (2) and (3) "do not apply
-- to an agreement to finance the operations and the carrying out of the functions of an office of the Fund in Singapore".
GIVEN `the Fund requested assistance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `another government has given or intends to give assistance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister gazetted the statement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the agreement includes grants` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Parliament fixed a maximum for grants` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it finances a Fund office in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `MAS may enter into the assistance agreement` IF
        `it finances a Fund office in Singapore`
    OR  (    `the Fund requested assistance`
         AND `another government has given or intends to give assistance`
         AND `the Minister gazetted the statement`
         AND (    (NOT `the agreement includes grants`)
              OR  `Parliament fixed a maximum for grants`))

-- s 6A(3): "It is not lawful for the Monetary Authority of Singapore to give any amount of grant under any agreement ... that is in
-- excess of the maximum amount fixed by Parliament". Read here as a cap on the total granted under the agreement (an inference: the
-- text does not say whether the cap is cumulative). (3A) lifts it for a Fund office in Singapore.
GIVEN `granted already` IS A NUMBER, `this grant` IS A NUMBER, `the Parliamentary maximum` IS A NUMBER,
      `it is for a Fund office in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant is lawful` IF
        `it is for a Fund office in Singapore`
    OR  `granted already` PLUS `this grant` AT MOST `the Parliamentary maximum`

-- s 6A(4): an agreement "to lend or give other financial assistance" MUST provide for MAS "to require early repayment or early
-- recovery" if the Fund arrangement or program is suspended or prematurely terminated. (5) [Act 20 of 2023]: not if (a) "the agreement
-- is in a standard form provided by the Fund, which cannot be unilaterally amended" by MAS; or (b) the arrangement or program "cannot
-- be suspended or prematurely terminated". Grants are not named in (4); (3A) does not disapply (4).
DECLARE Assistance IS ONE OF
    `a loan`
    `a grant`
    `other financial assistance`

GIVEN `the assistance` IS AN Assistance,
      `it is on a Fund standard form MAS cannot amend` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the arrangement cannot be suspended or terminated early` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement must provide for early repayment` IF
        (CONSIDER `the assistance`
         WHEN `a grant` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND (NOT `it is on a Fund standard form MAS cannot amend`)
    AND (NOT `the arrangement cannot be suspended or terminated early`)

§§ `7(3) -- the ceiling on the World Bank subscription`

-- s 7(3): "Except with the approval signified by resolution of Parliament, the subscription of Singapore shall not be increased so
-- that it (including any increases) exceeds the sum of US$40 million." No such ceiling is written for the Fund (s 4(2)).
GIVEN `the subscription now` IS A NUMBER, `the proposed increase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a resolution of Parliament is needed` IF
    `the subscription now` PLUS `the proposed increase` GREATER THAN 40000000

§§ `11, 12 -- orders, and the Bank outside the Companies Act`

-- s 11(1): the President "may, by order, make such provision as he may consider reasonably necessary for carrying into effect" the
-- Agreements, including the status, immunities and privileges of the Fund and Bank and their officers, "and the provisions of the
-- Fund Agreement with regard to the unenforceability of exchange contracts"; (2) an order "may declare that any specified provisions
-- of the Fund Agreement or the Bank Agreement shall have the force of law in Singapore". The Act itself enacts none of them.
GIVEN `an order under section 11 declares it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agreement provision has force of law through this Act` IF
    `an order under section 11 declares it`

-- s 12: the Bank "shall be deemed not to be a corporation within the meaning of the Companies Act 1967; and the provisions of that Act
-- shall not, accordingly, apply to the Bank or to the issue by the Bank of any shares, debentures, bonds, notes or other securities".
-- The section names the Bank only.
DECLARE Issuer IS ONE OF
    `the World Bank`
    `the IMF`
    `a Singapore company`

GIVEN `the issuer` IS AN Issuer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 12 takes the issue outside the Companies Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the issuer`
    WHEN `the World Bank` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `First Schedule -- terms of admission to the IMF`

-- para 1(c): "dollars" means "United States dollars of the weight and fineness in effect on July 1 1944". para 2: "The quota of
-- Singapore shall be $30 million." para 3: "The subscription of Singapore shall be equal to its quota. Singapore shall pay in gold,
-- as a minimum, 25% of its quota. The balance of the subscription shall be paid in the currency of Singapore."
GIVEN `quota` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum gold payment to the IMF` MEANS
    `quota` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `quota` IS A NUMBER, `gold paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the IMF balance payable in Singapore currency` MEANS
    `quota` MINUS `gold paid`

-- para 5: within 60 days of the Fund receiving the proposal, Singapore and the Fund "shall agree on an initial par value ...
-- provided that the Fund may extend the period of 60 days and that Singapore shall be deemed to have withdrawn from the Fund if
-- agreement on a par value has not been reached when the extended period expires". The deeming is tied to an EXTENDED period;
-- nothing is said of a 60-day period that was never extended. Days counted from the Fund's receipt; "expires" read as "more than
-- 60 + extension days have passed" (an inference about counting).
GIVEN `days since the Fund received the proposal` IS A NUMBER, `days of extension` IS A NUMBER, `a par value was agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore is deemed to have withdrawn from the Fund` IF
        `days of extension` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `days since the Fund received the proposal` GREATER THAN 60 PLUS `days of extension`
    AND (NOT `a par value was agreed`)

-- para 6: Singapore "may not engage in exchange transactions with the Fund until both (a) the par value ... has been agreed ... and
-- put into operation and (b) its subscription has been paid in full: provided, however, that ... the Executive Directors are
-- authorised to permit exchange transactions" earlier.
GIVEN `the par value is agreed and in operation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the subscription is paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Executive Directors permit it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore may transact with the Fund` IF
        (`the par value is agreed and in operation` AND `the subscription is paid in full`)
    OR  `the Executive Directors permit it`

-- paras 7, 8: Singapore becomes a member once the Fund has told the US Government that Singapore made the para 7 representation,
-- and Singapore has (a) deposited its instrument of acceptance with the US Government and (b) signed the original Articles.
GIVEN `the Fund informed the US Government` IS A BOOLEAN, `the instrument was deposited` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Articles were signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore is a member of the Fund` IF
    `the Fund informed the US Government` AND `the instrument was deposited` AND `the Articles were signed`

§§ `Second Schedule -- terms of admission to the World Bank`

-- para 2: Singapore "shall subscribe to 320 shares of the capital stock of the Bank at the par value of $100,000 per share". para 4:
-- (a) before accepting membership Singapore pays "on account of the subscription price of one-half of such shares" (i) gold or US
-- dollars "equal to 2% thereof" and (ii) its own currency "equal to 18% thereof"; (b) for the other half, the 2% and 18% portions
-- "shall be left uncalled". What becomes of the remaining 80% of each share is not said in the Schedule.
GIVEN `shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the World Bank subscription` MEANS
    `shares` TIMES 100000

GIVEN `shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gold or US dollar payment before membership` MEANS
    `shares` DIVIDED BY 2 TIMES 100000 TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Singapore currency payment before membership` MEANS
    `shares` DIVIDED BY 2 TIMES 100000 TIMES 18 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2 and 18 percent portions left uncalled` MEANS
    `shares` DIVIDED BY 2 TIMES 100000 TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100

-- para 3: "Before accepting membership in the Bank, Singapore shall accept membership in and become a member of the International
-- Monetary Fund." para 6: Singapore becomes a member when it has (a) become a Fund member; (b) made the para 4 payments; (c)
-- furnished the para 5 representation and information; (d) deposited its instrument of acceptance; and (e) signed the original
-- Articles.
GIVEN `a member of the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN, `the paragraph 4 payments were made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the representation was furnished` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Bank instrument was deposited` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Bank Articles were signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore is a member of the Bank` IF
        `a member of the Fund`
    AND `the paragraph 4 payments were made`
    AND `the representation was furnished`
    AND `the Bank instrument was deposited`
    AND `the Bank Articles were signed`
